#: <RELIC_ROOT>/docs/source/public/science/atmosphere.md
msgid "Site UV-A surface albedo alpha of J_NO2 = (1 + alpha) (B1 G + B2 G^2) (Trebs et al. 2009 Eq. 2); 0.03 is typical of grassland and vegetation (2-3 percent in the UV-A). The relation is not to be used for alpha > 0.2 (snow, ice, sand), which is the upper bound."
msgstr "J_NO2 = (1 + alpha) (B1 G + B2 G^2) 中的站点地表 UV-A 反照率 alpha（Trebs 等 2009，式 2）；0.03 是草地和植被的典型值（UV-A 波段约为 2-3%）。该关系不能用于 alpha > 0.2（雪、冰、沙地），因此 0.2 为上界。"

#: <RELIC_ROOT>/docs/source/public/science/atmosphere.md
msgid "Source: literature; Trebs, I., Bohn, B., Ammann, C., Rummel, U., Blumthaler, M., Konigstedt, R., Meixner, F.X., Fan, S. and Andreae, M.O. (2009) Relationship between the NO2 photolysis frequency and the solar global irradiance, Atmos. Meas. Tech. 2, 725-739, doi:10.5194/amt-2-725-2009; Sect. 4.6 and Table 1: UV-A surface albedo of vegetation about 2-3 percent, grassland 0.03 (Feister and Grewe 1995); the function should not be used for alpha > 0.2; Warneck, P. and Williams, J. (2012) The Atmospheric Chemist's Companion, Springer, doi:10.1007/978-94-007-2275-0; Table 6.7: ground-level photolysis frequencies for overhead sun and surface albedo 0.03 (Jacobson 2005)"
msgstr "来源：文献；Trebs, I., Bohn, B., Ammann, C., Rummel, U., Blumthaler, M., Konigstedt, R., Meixner, F.X., Fan, S. and Andreae, M.O. (2009) Relationship between the NO2 photolysis frequency and the solar global irradiance, Atmos. Meas. Tech. 2, 725-739, doi:10.5194/amt-2-725-2009; Sect. 4.6 and Table 1: UV-A surface albedo of vegetation about 2-3 percent, grassland 0.03 (Feister and Grewe 1995); the function should not be used for alpha > 0.2; Warneck, P. and Williams, J. (2012) The Atmospheric Chemist's Companion, Springer, doi:10.1007/978-94-007-2275-0; Table 6.7: ground-level photolysis frequencies for overhead sun and surface albedo 0.03 (Jacobson 2005)"

